| # `.ONESHELL` hands the whole recipe to one shell as one script, and a line
| # whose expansion came out empty is a BLANK LINE of that script rather than a
| # line that vanished: `chop_commands` (commands.c) never chopped the recipe, so
| # the newlines around the line are still where the makefile put them.
| #
| # A here-document is what makes that more than a blank line in an echo, because
| # there the script is reading its own text: the blank line is written into the
| # file. GNU Make 4.4.1 writes an empty line and then `line`; a build that drops
| # the line writes a different file.
| .ONESHELL:
| EMPTY =
| all:
| 	@cat <<'BODY' > out
| 	$(EMPTY)
| 	line
| 	BODY
